WEBVTT

00:32:58.540 --> 00:33:01.124
But when they debriefed about it,
the dynamic changed.

00:33:01.148 --> 00:33:03.983
Bess: I often talk to people
while I'm microwaving my lunch,

00:33:04.007 --> 00:33:06.384
and I always microwave my lunch
for three minutes.

00:33:06.408 --> 00:33:07.559
AG: That's Bess again.

00:33:07.583 --> 00:33:09.216
Bess: So I talk to people as long.

00:33:09.240 --> 00:33:12.205
Like, I often am like,
"Whoever's standing by the microwave

00:33:12.229 --> 00:33:13.724
talks to me for three minutes,"

00:33:13.748 --> 00:33:17.456
and then I'm like, "I guess I have to
go eat in my office by myself." (Laughs)

00:33:17.480 --> 00:33:19.520
Jessica: You don't have to
eat by yourself.

00:33:19.544 --> 00:33:21.509
Bess: I know! I don't know why I do that.

00:33:21.533 --> 00:33:23.298
Jessica: Come eat in the common room.

00:33:23.322 --> 00:33:24.494
Bess: I should do that.

00:33:25.570 --> 00:33:28.280
AG: If you want to build
a rapid high-quality connection,

00:33:28.304 --> 00:33:30.766
the research points to
a few effective strategies.